<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  Second Spectora "Export HTML Text" worksheet, used to prove the importer is driven by
  the header row rather than by the shape of the committed InterNACHI export.

  Deliberately different from sample-data/sheet1.xml in every way that could matter:

    * a different template (commercial rental walkthrough, not residential InterNACHI)
    * only 12 of the 42 columns the InterNACHI export carries - every optional column the
      importer models is absent, so the importer must not require them
    * an extra column the importer does not model at all ("Inspector Signature Required"),
      which must be ignored rather than rejected
    * a re-ordered "Order" column, to prove ordering comes from the export and not from
      row position
    * four deliberately dirty values that must each surface as an import issue instead of
      being silently coerced: an unknown Comment Type, an unknown Answer Type, a
      non-integer Category, and an out-of-range Category

  This is synthetic sample material for importer testing, not customer data.
-->
